  "readmeFile": "README.nuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "17.6.2: Fixes Umbraco Deploy imports of evaluator configurations being silently rolled back: read-only database scopes now complete, so they no longer cancel the surrounding Deploy (or other) transaction. 17.6.1: Adds Copilot tools: editors can evaluate the open page, get recommendations for failing checks and apply them after approving (values are staged, never saved); grant the Page Evaluator tool scopes per agent. Adds an evaluate_page agent tool and two optional add-on packages: ProWorks.Umbraco.AI.PageEvaluator.Automate (an \"Evaluate Page\" step for Umbraco Automate) and ProWorks.Umbraco.AI.PageEvaluator.Deploy (Umbraco Deploy support for evaluator configurations). Also: the 10-per-minute evaluation limit now applies to every caller without app.UseRateLimiter(); fixes intermittent \"database is locked\" errors when saving, activating or deleting evaluator configurations on SQLite. API change: GET /evaluate/cached/{nodeId} now answers 204 No Content when there is no cached result (was 404); 404 now only means the page doesn't exist.",
